    "option": "religion:civicoption_religion",
    "pedia": "A \u0022personality cult\u0022 is the creation of an idealized or even worshipful image of a person through propaganda and mass media. Leaders had nearly always been held as revered figures in history, and some were deified either in life or in death, while others claimed to hold their rule through the \u0022divine right of kings\u0022. After the rise of rationalism and secularism, this ideal became harder to preserve. The development of propaganda techniques allowed leaders, especially in totalitarian states, to manipulate their image in new ways. These cults were often so strong as to be practically religions.",
